Prince Charles is the latest famous face  to test positive for the coronavirus  according to a palace spokesperson a 71  year old royal has not been to the  hospital his symptoms are mild and he's  in good spirits  in fact a source tells ET that the  Prince of Wales is quote doing well for  the palace Charles took the Cova 19 test  on Monday and his results came back  positive the following day Tuesday he  and his wife Camilla are currently  quarantined at their estate in Scotland  although the Duchess moved to another  area of the home to self isolate  following her husband's diagnosis  Camilla was also tested her results came  back negative  the palace confirms that the Duke and  Duchess of Cornwall remain in touch with  their families and Charles has notified  both his sons Prince William and Harry  the famous family was last seen together  publicly on March 9th at the  Commonwealth Day service at Westminster  Abbey according to the palace it's  impossible to determine who Charles  caught the virus from given the high  number of public engagements he's  carried out in recent weeks and the  preventative no handshake policy that  hasn't always been easy for Charles to  remember that was the 71 year old at the  National Prince's Trust Awards on March  11th now as for the Queen the palace  reports that she remains in good health  adding that she last saw Charles briefly  on the morning of March 12th the 93 year  old monarch is said to be following  advice regarding her health including  moving to Windsor Castle on March 19th  one week earlier than planned  [Music]
 

